## 2. Context loading

- **Coding conventions** → `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` scoped with `applyTo`, so they load only for matching files (e.g. Razor → `Pages/**`, EF → `Data/**`, tests → `tests/**`).
- **Procedures** → skills that load only when relevant (Windows Server deploy, EF migrations, Jenkins job).
- **Agent files** say what to read and when ("read X only if Y"); they don't copy docs into themselves.
- **Fresh context per role:** start each role in a new session or subagent, passing only the plan path.

---

## 3. Workflow and roles

### 3.1 Roles

| Agent | Change | Loads |
|---|---|---|
| Architect | Keeps planning; sole writer of reference docs | Overview, relevant component doc, decisions |
| Developer | **Merge backend + frontend** — a Razor Pages feature spans PageModel, view and service | Plan, relevant component doc, scoped instructions |
| Tester | Stays separate | Plan (acceptance criteria, test cases), diff, `testing.md` |
| Reviewer | Stays separate | Diff, plan acceptance criteria, review checklist — not architecture docs |
| Security | On demand, triggered by plan flag (see 4) | Diff, plan, `security.md` |

### 3.2 Doc updates

- Only the architect updates reference docs, at feature close, rewriting rather than appending.
- Developer, tester, reviewer and security write only into the plan, including a `Doc impact` line.

### 3.3 Plan template

```markdown
# <Feature>

## Goal
## Non-goals
## Component(s) affected
## Decisions
<!-- one line each, or link -->
## Tasks
- [ ] Task — acceptance criteria
## Test cases
## Security review
required | not needed — reason
## Doc impact
none | one line per affected doc
## Status log
<!-- one short entry per agent, capped -->
## Review findings
<!-- severity — finding — one-line fix -->
```

---

## 4. Security agent

- **Context:** diff + plan + short `security.md` (trust boundaries, auth, where secrets live, accepted risks). Checklist lives in the agent file or a skill, not in the docs.
- **Trigger:** the plan's `Security review` field, set by the architect. Required when a change touches auth or roles, file upload/download, external input, secrets, or a new endpoint.
- **Scope:** diff by default; full-audit mode before a release.
- **No overlap:** remove security items from the general reviewer's checklist.
- **Findings:** severity + one-line fix in the plan's review section. Accepted risks get one line in `security.md` so later runs don't re-raise them.

### Hub-specific checklist

- [ ] Bundle zips: path traversal on extract (zip slip), size and zip-bomb limits, content-type on download.
- [ ] Authorization: fallback policy so no page is anonymous by mistake; role checks on admin actions.
- [ ] Users can't change other users' votes or favourites.
- [ ] Anti-forgery tokens on vote and favourite POST handlers.
- [ ] XSS if asset metadata or markdown from repos is rendered.
- [ ] GitLab tokens (report generator, assets CI) kept in Jenkins/GitLab credentials, not config files.
- [ ] CSV injection if the catalogue CSV is opened in Excel.

